    text+='\n\n## CP35 bounded closure and actual remaining work\n\n430 registered CPU results and all 22 combined stages pass; fmt and final normal/QA Clippy/build pass. Native Story and character/library editor flows pass normal/small, including injected pre-mutation save faults with exact edited-source/media retention. Reload/folder actions now use common accessible tooltip icon buttons; library folder field follows available width. Character save error visibility was corrected after actual screenshot inspection.\n\nG7 uses Node only as an optional native ECMAScript filter engine; source-executed Director oracle covers UTF-16, escape, class, backreference, invalid-inline-flag and duplicate-name semantics. Cache/repaint/stale-result/child-reap/missing-engine/manual-Apply tests pass. Normal/small actual UI catalog selection reaches the synthetic worker with the expected effective stack. This is not GPU patch numerics or full Python inference parity.\n\nNo general publication readiness is claimed. Image-workspace sampling preview and Exp prefix/continuation remain actual implementation gaps; broader conditioning/Python/memory and older rich formats plus common final UI/keyboard/OS chooser acceptance remain as listed above. Specific denied Exp3step/log operations remain forbidden. No GPU, additional cleanup, product activation, storage migration or user-process restart in CP35.\n'
